    pm:nameForm "sekhet-hra-asht-aru" ;
    pm:nameRole "doorkeeper of the first arit" ;
    skos:definition "One of the three officers of the first of the seven arits. The chapter gives the three names and nothing else about them: the dead man is told the name of the doorkeeper, the name of the watcher and the name of the herald, and then says his address."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:EgyptianRitual ;
    dcterms:source "Book of the Dead, chapter 147, the first arit, Papyrus of Ani (British Museum No. 10,470, sheets 11 and 12), in the English of E. A. Wallis Budge, London: Kegan Paul, Trench, Trübner, 1901, vol. II, pp. 473-479" .

